# 2026-11-04, one by-hand row on Google's lab Galaxy S26 units (Developer Device Platform pool m1q-36,
# SM-S942U1; android/ddp/devices.json), not a page row: the campaign name holds no `dashboard`, so the dashboard page never
# reads it as a weekly sitting, and the lab units' weekly stand-in rows stay the s26-ddp slot's.
# litert-community/Qwen3.5-0.8B (Qwen3.5-0.8B_int8.litertlm, Hub main LFS sha256 25447e25..., 964,566,992 B) on the
# protocol row, native-benchmark-1024x256 = litert_lm_advanced_main --benchmark, prefill forced to exactly
# 1024 tokens, decode 256, context 2048 (methodology/agreed-protocol-gemma4.md "The spec"), LiteRT-LM GPU on the flat
# pinned build v0.19.0 (commit 771b06e1; its GPU accelerator built from source and linked into the binary:
# "Statically linked GPU accelerator").
# This row = matrices/d543-qwen35-s26-gpu-flat-android.cells' row (the attached Galaxy S26 SM-S942Q, 2026-11-04)
# with runs=3 instead of runs=1: one Device Run job = three launches on one lab unit, one benchmark per process,
# the wrapper's 120 s cooldown and thermal gate before runs 2 and 3; run 1 builds the GPU program cache (firstEver).
# The round's other builds: matrices/d552-qwen35-ddp-s26-pregpu-android.cells and
# matrices/d552-qwen35-ddp-s26-public-android.cells (their own campaigns: engine-build= is not part of the cell key).
# Run: ./bench matrix <this file> --ddp m1q-36 --campaign 2026-11-04-d552-qwen35-ddp-s26-flat
android litert-lm litert-community/Qwen3.5-0.8B native-benchmark-1024x256 backend=gpu file=Qwen3.5-0.8B_int8.litertlm context-tokens=2048 runs=3
